    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a practical tool, not something abstract. Growing up in a family where my parents had different educational backgrounds—my mom with a master’s and dad with a vocational diploma—helped me appreciate how math applies to real life, like budgeting for our family or understanding physics concepts in cooking. I use it daily without stress.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I rarely feel anxious about math because I’ve built confidence through hands-on practice. My hobbies like cooking and board games involve problem-solving, which helps me stay calm. When I do get nervous, it’s usually about applying complex concepts quickly, not the math itself.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a math app to check my algebra homework last year. It explained steps clearly and showed me where I went wrong. The app was helpful but I preferred using it for verification rather than full solutions, as I wanted to build my own understanding.",
