    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized practice problems that adapt to a student’s level, offering instant feedback on mistakes. They can also explain concepts in simple language, like breaking down calculus steps. This helps students learn at their own pace without feeling overwhelmed, making math more accessible and engaging."
